00:14:23,540 --> 00:14:25,775
Let's see you give me my tough lesson.

247
00:14:27,280 --> 00:14:29,617
Why should I show you my card after you've

248
00:14:29,700 --> 00:14:32,465
gone to such lengths to
keep yours in the dark?

249
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:34,400
I think you're stalling.

250
00:14:34,640 --> 00:14:36,017
You don't trust me, Panic?

251
00:14:36,100 --> 00:14:39,629
Believe it or not, not all
duelists are lying dogs like you.

252
00:14:40,940 --> 00:14:42,764
And to prove it, I'll show you.

253
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:46,637
After all, I wouldn't want you
thinking I was some kind of liar.

254
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:47,560
Show me.

255
00:14:48,060 --> 00:14:51,178
You don't need to prove
anything to that slime, Yugi.

256
00:14:51,780 --> 00:14:53,600
Ready, Panic? Here it is.

257
00:14:54,020 --> 00:14:55,900
The Swords of Revealing Light.

258
00:14:59,260 --> 00:15:00,137
Revealing Light?

259
00:15:00,220 --> 00:15:03,577
The blinding magic of the Swords
of Revealing Light not only

260
00:15:03,660 --> 00:15:07,037
stops all enemy monsters from
attacking for three full turns,

261
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:10,497
but it bathes the entire
field in a light so luminous

262
00:15:10,580 --> 00:15:13,874
that even your lurking shadow
creatures will be exposed.

263
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:21,035
Soon, Panic, the monsters in your
dark empire will have nowhere to hide.

264
00:15:21,140 --> 00:15:22,557
But rather than play it now,

265
00:15:22,640 --> 00:15:26,997
I'll take a page from your book and let
you worry about when and how I'll use it,

266
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:30,374
just like you do with the
monsters you hide in the dark.

267
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:33,260
You're going down in five turns.

268
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:34,920
Five turns, Panic.

269
00:15:35,740 --> 00:15:38,160
Then my monsters will finish you off.

270
00:15:38,500 --> 00:15:40,960
Curse of Dragon, Defensive Mode.

271
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:45,460
And, of course, the card that
will make you see the light.

272
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:49,660
Your five turns start now, Panic.

273
00:15:49,880 --> 00:15:50,980
It's your move.

274
00:15:52,460 --> 00:15:53,880
He's taunting me.

275
00:15:54,140 --> 00:15:56,820
That must be the Swords
of Revealing Light.

276
00:15:57,620 --> 00:15:59,091
What's the matter, Panic?

277
00:15:59,220 --> 00:16:01,000
Has bullying lost its thrill?

278
00:16:01,280 --> 00:16:02,960
I'll teach you about Bloss.

279
00:16:03,140 --> 00:16:03,980
Just you wait.

280
00:16:04,580 --> 00:16:09,109
Hey, Mai, why is Yugi keeping that card
out if he's not going to play it yet?

281
00:16:10,540 --> 00:16:14,520
Uh, I hate to say it, guys,
but it's not a good sign. Huh?

282
00:16:15,260 --> 00:16:18,217
I was able to keep it together
for about this long, too.

283
00:16:18,300 --> 00:16:22,597
But after a while, Panic has a way of
getting to you and making you slip up.

284
00:16:22,680 --> 00:16:23,840
Not my pal.

285
00:16:24,080 --> 00:16:25,477
He knows what he's doing.

286
00:16:25,560 --> 00:16:26,760
I sure hope so.

287
00:16:27,280 --> 00:16:28,120
He does.

288
00:16:28,680 --> 00:16:32,798
Listen, I know Yugi's good, but
fighting Panic isn't about being good.

289
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:34,697
It's about keeping a
level head while you're

290
00:16:34,780 --> 00:16:37,309
lost in the dark or
being attacked by fire.

291
00:16:37,940 --> 00:16:42,480
Yugi's gonna need guts to win
this duel, not skill. Guts, huh?

292
00:16:42,700 --> 00:16:43,960
Well, he's got heart.

293
00:16:44,280 --> 00:16:45,398
You got that right.

294
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:49,417
Yes, but he did just leave his
best card out fully vulnerable.

295
00:16:49,500 --> 00:16:52,737
You don't make those kinds of
mistakes unless you're nervous.

296
00:16:52,820 --> 00:16:56,408
And Panic's not one to let a
mistake like that go unpunished.

297
00:16:57,500 --> 00:16:59,080
Make your move, Panic!

298
00:17:02,140 --> 00:17:03,400
I must say,

299
00:17:03,620 --> 00:17:07,577
it was quite a daring move to illuminate
me with the presence of that card,

300
00:17:07,660 --> 00:17:08,490
little Yugi.

301
00:17:09,120 --> 00:17:13,473
But it was a critical mistake to leave
it on the field completely exposed.

302
00:17:15,020 --> 00:17:19,260
If you thought idle cards were safe
from attacks, you were dead wrong!

303
00:17:21,660 --> 00:17:23,880
Reaper of the Cards!

304
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:25,510
The Reaper?

305
00:17:26,380 --> 00:17:29,117
when the reaper has summoned
all magic cards hear the

306
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:32,597
ghostly toll of doom he'll be
sending your revealing light

307
00:17:32,680 --> 00:17:36,497
card to the discard graveyard
leaving you defenseless

308
00:17:36,580 --> 00:17:42,260
reaper attack yugi but that
card was yugi's only chance

309
00:17:51,080 --> 00:17:56,240
Your fate belongs to me now,
Yugi Call of the Graveyard

310
00:18:06,220 --> 00:18:07,700
What's going on?

311
00:18:10,360 --> 00:18:12,120
It can't finish its attack

312
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:19,537
it should have destroyed
your card the swords

313
00:18:19,620 --> 00:18:22,617
of revealing light I said
my swords of revealing

314
00:18:22,700 --> 00:18:24,557
light is the card that
would illuminate your

315
00:18:24,640 --> 00:18:27,217
monsters I never said
it was the one I placed

316
00:18:27,300 --> 00:18:30,317
on the field you just assumed that but if

317
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:32,977
that's not the card I
placed on the field was a

318
00:18:33,060 --> 00:18:37,377
different card the spell
binding circle a trap

319
00:18:37,460 --> 00:18:43,020
card yes a trap card
that snares your reaper,

320
00:18:43,180 --> 00:18:45,062
stopping him dead in his tracks,

321
00:18:45,460 --> 00:18:47,519
encircling him in a magical prison.

322
00:18:50,040 --> 00:18:51,320
In Duel Monsters,

323
00:18:51,440 --> 00:18:53,717
one must be wary of the
reaper of the cards and

324
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:56,859
its ability to send magic
cards to the discard pile.

325
00:18:57,160 --> 00:19:01,017
I figured that you probably had one
stalking around in your deck somewhere.

326
00:19:01,100 --> 00:19:04,100
But now that he's frozen,
unable to damage my deck,

327
00:19:04,280 --> 00:19:08,700
I'm free to lay whatever magic cards
I want on the field. Great thinking!

328
00:19:08,940 --> 00:19:10,457
Way to put one over on him, Youg!

329
00:19:10,540 --> 00:19:12,140
What is it with this kid?

330
00:19:12,340 --> 00:19:15,157
I can't even keep up with
him here on the sidelines.

331
00:19:15,240 --> 00:19:17,560
He's doing good, but it's not over yet.

332
00:19:21,440 --> 00:19:22,817
How dare you!

333
00:19:22,900 --> 00:19:24,320
You fooled me!

334
00:19:25,040 --> 00:19:29,340
You fooled yourself, Panic, and
wasted quite a powerful card, too.

335
00:19:29,640 --> 00:19:35,200
But now that the coast is clear, I'll
really lay my Swords of Revealing Light!

336
00:19:38,520 --> 00:19:40,340
And a second magic card.

337
00:19:41,340 --> 00:19:42,840
Both face down.

338
00:19:45,540 --> 00:19:46,980
Face down? Why?

339
00:19:47,840 --> 00:19:49,140
Now what's up?

340
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:53,560
I don't know, but I bet we're
going to find out soon enough.

341
00:19:54,100 --> 00:19:54,930
So what?

342
00:19:55,080 --> 00:19:58,962
You captured my Reaper, but he's
only one of my powerful monsters.

343
00:19:59,140 --> 00:20:01,560
The ones that remain will destroy you!
